1
00:00:00,465 --> 00:00:04,465
[bright music]

2
00:00:28,848 --> 00:00:32,848
[bright music]

3
00:01:27,192 --> 00:01:31,192
[bright music]

4
00:01:39,958 --> 00:01:41,458
Bestfriend,

5
00:01:41,791 --> 00:01:43,125
with me,

6
00:01:43,416 --> 00:01:45,666
there's no need for teasing anymore.

7
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:47,541
What?

8
00:01:47,583 --> 00:01:49,291
I'm not teasing you.

9
00:01:51,375 --> 00:01:53,541
The heat here in the US is unbearable.

10
00:01:53,583 --> 00:01:56,583
I thought it’s always freezing in America!

11
00:01:56,625 --> 00:01:58,250
Yeah, that's what I thought too.

12
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:01,708
I thought that you were
topless solely for my sake.

13
00:02:03,125 --> 00:02:05,624
What are you doing, bestfriend?

14
00:02:05,666 --> 00:02:07,333
Isn't it obvious?

15
00:02:07,375 --> 00:02:08,583
I'm cooking.

16
00:02:08,625 --> 00:02:09,749
Wow!

17
00:02:09,791 --> 00:02:12,250
My crush is so impressive!

18
00:02:14,208 --> 00:02:16,452
So delightful!

19
00:02:16,494 --> 00:02:19,166
[laughter]

20
00:02:19,208 --> 00:02:20,999
So aside from working as a cashier,

21
00:02:21,041 --> 00:02:23,625
you're also a part-time chef?

22
00:02:23,875 --> 00:02:26,333
Let's just say, this is my way
of repaying back my roommate

23
00:02:26,375 --> 00:02:28,291
for everything he’s done for me.

24
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:31,250
Repay? Repay my a♪♪!

25
00:02:31,666 --> 00:02:33,583
You’re in love, idiot!

26
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:39,750
Wow, bestfriend!

27
00:02:39,958 --> 00:02:43,250
It's been a long time since
I've seen you so inspired.

28
00:02:43,708 --> 00:02:46,458
So when can I expect to meet the lucky one?

29
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:49,166
He's not ready for that yet, bestfriend.

30
00:02:49,333 --> 00:02:50,791
But don't worry,

31
00:02:50,833 --> 00:02:52,583
I'm gonna do my best to convince him.

32
00:02:53,291 --> 00:02:54,958
Bring him to the Philippines.

33
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:57,625
Let's see if he meets my standards.

34
00:02:58,166 --> 00:03:00,250
Sure, I'll put him in my suitcase.

35
00:03:00,791 --> 00:03:02,249
Is that possible?

36
00:03:02,291 --> 00:03:04,458
Won’t you get arrested at the airport?

37
00:03:05,416 --> 00:03:06,541
Fine,

38
00:03:06,583 --> 00:03:08,875
I'll keep him here, instead.

39
00:03:10,500 --> 00:03:12,750
You amaze me, bestfriend!

40
00:03:13,333 --> 00:03:15,749
But let me remind you
to take things slowly.

41
00:03:15,791 --> 00:03:19,416
If that doesn't lead to a happy
ending, you might get depressed again.

42
00:03:19,458 --> 00:03:21,958
And then you’ll start
doing weird things again.

43
00:03:22,250 --> 00:03:24,416
And why would we not have a happy ending?

44
00:03:24,458 --> 00:03:27,458
Because you’re going back to
the Philippines in a few weeks,

45
00:03:27,500 --> 00:03:30,166
so you'll be embarking on
another long-distance relationship!

46
00:03:30,208 --> 00:03:33,041
Then you'll find yourself
missing him constantly.

47
00:03:33,083 --> 00:03:35,458
And eventually, he'll
get frustrated with you

48
00:03:35,500 --> 00:03:38,541
and decide to break up
because of your clinginess.

49
00:03:38,583 --> 00:03:44,375
You’ll once again blame yourself,
saying you’re not enough, whatsoever.

50
00:03:45,208 --> 00:03:48,708
So where’s your happy ending now?

51
00:03:49,625 --> 00:03:52,458
You're so obssesed
with long-distance affairs.

52
00:03:52,666 --> 00:03:54,624
There are plenty of cute
people in the Philippines.

53
00:03:54,666 --> 00:03:56,541
Why not choose someone from here?

54
00:03:59,750 --> 00:04:01,000
I don't know, bestfriend.

55
00:04:01,541 --> 00:04:03,208
I'd rather not dwell on it for now.

56
00:04:03,416 --> 00:04:05,875
I'll just enjoy every
moment we have together.

57
00:04:06,541 --> 00:04:07,749
Do as you please.

58
00:04:07,791 --> 00:04:10,500
Just remember, I did warn you.

59
00:04:11,541 --> 00:04:13,291
But worse comes to worst,

60
00:04:13,875 --> 00:04:16,083
you'll always be there for me, right?

61
00:04:17,625 --> 00:04:19,041
Here we go again.

62
00:04:19,833 --> 00:04:22,208
You only remember me when...

63
00:04:22,250 --> 00:04:23,833
you’re brokenhearted!

64
00:04:29,212 --> 00:04:33,212
[playful music]

65
00:04:41,041 --> 00:04:42,166
Hi, babe.

66
00:04:42,541 --> 00:04:44,041
What did just you call me?

67
00:04:45,666 --> 00:04:46,266
Nothing.

68
00:04:46,916 --> 00:04:47,958
Anyways, uh,

69
00:04:48,125 --> 00:04:49,750
I made lunch for you.

70
00:04:49,916 --> 00:04:52,958
Yeah, how am I supposed
to eat while I’m driving?

71
00:04:53,833 --> 00:04:54,433
Um,

72
00:04:54,916 --> 00:04:56,833
maybe in between passengers?

73
00:04:57,083 --> 00:04:59,291
When I’m in between
passengers, I’m still driving.

74
00:05:01,791 --> 00:05:04,250
Okay, I just did something nice for you.

75
00:05:04,500 --> 00:05:05,833
I didn't ask you to.

76
00:05:07,333 --> 00:05:09,916
Yeah, well, maybe instead of
complaining, you could just say

77
00:05:10,250 --> 00:05:11,416
thank you.

78
00:05:11,541 --> 00:05:15,500
- Thank you for being so kind,
generous - - Fine, thank you.

79
00:05:15,791 --> 00:05:17,083
Don’t call me babe.

80
00:05:17,875 --> 00:05:18,833
Okay.

81
00:05:20,083 --> 00:05:22,708
And you could also say thank you,

82
00:05:22,750 --> 00:05:27,958
I’m just so lucky to have someone
who does small nice things for me.

83
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:29,708
I’ll pick you up at ten.

84
00:05:34,521 --> 00:05:38,521
[bright music]

85
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:54,600
Oh.

86
00:05:55,250 --> 00:05:56,916
Hi, how can I help you?

87
00:05:56,958 --> 00:05:59,166
I'm looking for a crew
member who works here.

88
00:05:59,666 --> 00:06:01,124
Oh, it's just me.

89
00:06:01,166 --> 00:06:02,666
It’s my shift until closing.

90
00:06:02,708 --> 00:06:04,166
How about the one before you?

91
00:06:04,625 --> 00:06:06,374
- The one before me? - Yeah.

92
00:06:06,416 --> 00:06:08,083
Oh, he resigned last week.

93
00:06:08,500 --> 00:06:09,583
Really?

94
00:06:10,125 --> 00:06:11,041
Yeap.

95
00:06:12,416 --> 00:06:13,916
Where is he working now?

96
00:06:14,708 --> 00:06:15,791
No idea.

97
00:06:17,250 --> 00:06:18,708
He's really avoiding me.

98
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:23,124
Anyway, um, thank you for your time.

99
00:06:23,166 --> 00:06:24,583
Yeah, no worries.

100
00:06:33,214 --> 00:06:37,214
[street noise]

101
00:06:57,375 --> 00:06:58,708
Oh, hey!

102
00:06:59,416 --> 00:07:00,499
You found me!

103
00:07:00,541 --> 00:07:02,541
Yeah, it’s a small apartment.

104
00:07:02,583 --> 00:07:04,125
It’s not very hard.

105
00:07:05,541 --> 00:07:06,750
How's your night?

106
00:07:07,291 --> 00:07:07,958
Nothing new.

107
00:07:09,458 --> 00:07:11,625
Did you eat the food I made you?

108
00:07:12,291 --> 00:07:13,666
Yeah, it was okay.

109
00:07:15,166 --> 00:07:15,875
Ah,

110
00:07:16,166 --> 00:07:17,125
excuse me.

111
00:07:17,333 --> 00:07:19,083
That’s adobo you’re talking about.

112
00:07:20,125 --> 00:07:20,791
And?

113
00:07:21,166 --> 00:07:23,791
And adobo isn’t just okay.

114
00:07:24,166 --> 00:07:26,833
That’s our national food.
Everybody loves adobo!

115
00:07:27,083 --> 00:07:28,166
Okay, fine.

116
00:07:28,208 --> 00:07:29,166
I loved it.

117
00:07:29,208 --> 00:07:32,375
It was the best thing I’ve
ever had in my entire life.

118
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:38,125
Love your sincerity.

119
00:07:39,083 --> 00:07:42,041
By the way, the store manager texted me.

120
00:07:42,083 --> 00:07:44,833
They have people covering
the shifts all weekend

121
00:07:44,875 --> 00:07:47,083
so they’re not gonna need
us tomorrow or Sunday.

122
00:07:48,958 --> 00:07:51,291
Oh, okay. So does that mean that -

123
00:07:51,333 --> 00:07:54,166
Yeah, um, you’re losing two days of work

124
00:07:54,208 --> 00:07:57,916
which is like 140 dollars for you.

125
00:07:58,083 --> 00:07:59,708
That's... That’s not what I was gonna say.

126
00:08:00,291 --> 00:08:01,291
What were you gonna say?

127
00:08:04,375 --> 00:08:07,416
Well, you know, we’re
both gonna be off for a day.

128
00:08:07,458 --> 00:08:08,583
Maybe we could…

129
00:08:09,416 --> 00:08:10,583
go to a few places?

130
00:08:10,625 --> 00:08:12,000
Well, who said I’m gonna be off?

131
00:08:13,541 --> 00:08:16,958
I might end up just picking
up some shifts driving.

132
00:08:22,143 --> 00:08:26,143
[bright music]

133
00:08:35,708 --> 00:08:36,583
Good morning.

134
00:08:37,625 --> 00:08:38,875
Good morning.

135
00:08:39,625 --> 00:08:40,708
Who's that for?

136
00:08:41,541 --> 00:08:42,625
It's just for us.

137
00:08:44,291 --> 00:08:45,625
That’s nice.

138
00:08:45,875 --> 00:08:48,291
But I told you I have to
go right to work today.

139
00:08:48,916 --> 00:08:52,000
Yeah, I know. But you still need to eat.

140
00:09:02,208 --> 00:09:02,833
Oh,

141
00:09:03,041 --> 00:09:04,458
why are you still here? Go shower.

142
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:05,916
Food will be ready in a few minutes.

143
00:09:09,291 --> 00:09:10,708
Where did you wanna go today?

144
00:09:12,083 --> 00:09:12,791
Um,

145
00:09:12,958 --> 00:09:14,041
I don’t know.

146
00:09:14,166 --> 00:09:15,833
I googled several places to go to

147
00:09:15,875 --> 00:09:18,375
but they’re hard to get to
when you’re commuting so...

148
00:09:18,875 --> 00:09:21,041
I’ll probably just end up in the
Hollywood Walk of Fame again.

149
00:09:21,500 --> 00:09:22,833
Who says you’re commuting?

150
00:09:23,625 --> 00:09:25,833
Well, hello, I don’t have a car.

151
00:09:26,041 --> 00:09:26,916
I know.

152
00:09:27,375 --> 00:09:28,333
But I do.

153
00:09:28,666 --> 00:09:30,625
Yeah, but you have work and I…

154
00:09:36,500 --> 00:09:37,125
Oh.

155
00:09:41,125 --> 00:09:42,583
I’m gonna go shower.

156
00:09:44,250 --> 00:09:45,625
W…Wait.

157
00:09:46,958 --> 00:09:47,749
What?

158
00:09:47,791 --> 00:09:49,124
Mind if I join?

159
00:09:49,166 --> 00:09:50,666
Do you want me to go right to work?

160
00:09:50,708 --> 00:09:51,541
Nah.

161
00:09:52,208 --> 00:09:54,458
No need to make any rash decisions.

162
00:09:59,500 --> 00:10:01,541
I'm serious you should come back with me.

163
00:10:02,041 --> 00:10:04,625
There's a lot of Koreans
in the Philippines.

164
00:10:05,333 --> 00:10:07,458
If I wanna be around
Koreans, I'd go to Korea.

165
00:10:10,370 --> 00:10:14,370
[bright music]

166
00:10:23,083 --> 00:10:25,875
I'm gonna miss this when I
go back to the Philippines.

167
00:10:26,291 --> 00:10:27,666
When's your flight?

168
00:10:27,708 --> 00:10:28,874
I knew it.

169
00:10:28,916 --> 00:10:31,041
You just can’t wait to get rid of me.

170
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:32,666
You're the one who just said

171
00:10:32,708 --> 00:10:34,874
"I'm gonna miss this
when I'm in the Philippines"

172
00:10:34,916 --> 00:10:36,416
blah blah blah.

173
00:10:38,708 --> 00:10:39,624
What?

174
00:10:39,666 --> 00:10:41,000
Why are you lauging?

175
00:10:41,750 --> 00:10:43,249
Can you say that again?

176
00:10:43,291 --> 00:10:44,458
Say what?

177
00:10:45,125 --> 00:10:46,833
Blah blah blah.

178
00:10:46,875 --> 00:10:48,500
Are you mocking me?

179
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:50,041
No,

180
00:10:50,625 --> 00:10:53,416
I just think you're really
cute when you say it.

181
00:10:53,916 --> 00:10:54,833
Shut up.

182
00:10:56,208 --> 00:10:57,833
Come on, one more. Just for me.

183
00:10:57,875 --> 00:11:00,208
- Blah blah blah. - Stop it.

184
00:11:03,666 --> 00:11:05,041
You know what?

185
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:08,958
You should come with me
when I go back to the Philippines.

186
00:11:09,333 --> 00:11:10,833
Are you crazy?

187
00:11:11,166 --> 00:11:12,583
Not anymore than usual.

188
00:11:14,333 --> 00:11:16,500
I’m serious. You should come back with me.

189
00:11:16,833 --> 00:11:19,875
There’s... a lot of
Koreans in the Philippines.

190
00:11:20,083 --> 00:11:22,291
If I wanna be around
Koreans, I’d go to Korea.

191
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:25,333
Yeah, but I wouldn’t be there.

192
00:11:25,791 --> 00:11:26,958
Thank God.

193
00:11:27,014 --> 00:11:28,916
[bright music]

194
00:11:28,958 --> 00:11:30,124
Really?

195
00:11:30,166 --> 00:11:31,791
Yeah, really.

196
00:11:32,666 --> 00:11:34,083
I don’t buy it.

197
00:11:34,125 --> 00:11:37,458
I think the second I leave,
you’re gonna be crying on the floor,

198
00:11:37,500 --> 00:11:39,208
begging me to come back.

199
00:11:39,250 --> 00:11:40,458
You wish.

200
00:11:40,500 --> 00:11:42,208
I’d be relieved.

201
00:11:44,125 --> 00:11:45,250
Come with me.

202
00:11:50,750 --> 00:11:52,208
What would I do for work?

203
00:11:53,666 --> 00:11:55,125
Don’t worry about it.

204
00:11:55,416 --> 00:11:57,750
We would... figure something out.

205
00:11:58,333 --> 00:12:02,500
Why wouldn’t I worry?
I’d be in a foreign country.

206
00:12:03,208 --> 00:12:05,749
Yeah. But we would be together.

207
00:12:05,791 --> 00:12:08,625
And that would be enough.

208
00:12:13,125 --> 00:12:14,208
Wow.

209
00:12:16,875 --> 00:12:18,375
That’s so dumb.

210
00:12:27,932 --> 00:12:31,932
[bright music]

211
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:40,374
So are all Filipinos this romantic?

212
00:12:40,416 --> 00:12:41,583
Or is it just you?

213
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:45,916
Well, we have like a
hundred romcoms every year.

214
00:12:46,416 --> 00:12:47,541
There it is.

215
00:12:50,333 --> 00:12:51,666
Speaking of romantic,

216
00:12:51,708 --> 00:12:55,541
there was actually a customer who
came into the liquor store yesterday,

217
00:12:55,583 --> 00:12:58,666
asking about the last crew who resigned.

218
00:12:58,708 --> 00:13:01,999
I don’t know if they were exes.

219
00:13:02,041 --> 00:13:05,500
And I didn’t really know who
exactly he was looking for but…

220
00:13:06,583 --> 00:13:08,166
that was kinda romantic –

221
00:13:09,250 --> 00:13:13,541
to be spending all that time
looking for someone you miss.

222
00:13:16,541 --> 00:13:18,916
But maybe I have it all wrong.

223
00:13:18,958 --> 00:13:23,250
Maybe the crew member who
resigned just owes the customer money.

224
00:13:23,583 --> 00:13:24,500
Or

225
00:13:24,875 --> 00:13:28,083
Maybe they’re part of the mafia
or some underground operation.

226
00:13:28,833 --> 00:13:30,333
What do you think?

227
00:13:31,500 --> 00:13:32,499
You said

228
00:13:32,541 --> 00:13:35,083
he was looking for the
crew member that resigned?

229
00:13:35,833 --> 00:13:36,916
Yeap,

230
00:13:36,958 --> 00:13:40,916
which assumed means it's
the one who I replaced, right?

231
00:13:42,758 --> 00:13:44,333
[bright music]

232
00:13:44,375 --> 00:13:46,166
Can you help me with something later?

233
00:13:47,625 --> 00:13:48,791
Yeah, sure.

234
00:13:57,041 --> 00:13:59,083
Uh, this is a lot.

235
00:13:59,875 --> 00:14:01,041
Will you help me fold these?

236
00:14:01,375 --> 00:14:02,166
Sure.

237
00:14:02,208 --> 00:14:03,041
Thanks.

238
00:14:13,541 --> 00:14:15,499
Do you use to work in retail or something?

239
00:14:15,541 --> 00:14:16,541
No. Why?

240
00:14:17,291 --> 00:14:19,208
You're like really good at that.

241
00:14:19,250 --> 00:14:23,250
Well, my mom used to do
other people’s laundry for a living.

242
00:14:23,791 --> 00:14:25,916
And I help her sometimes.

243
00:14:26,500 --> 00:14:31,458
There wasn’t really a reliable
source of water where we lived so

244
00:14:32,125 --> 00:14:34,333
she would do the laundry by a river.

245
00:14:35,291 --> 00:14:36,791
By hand.

246
00:14:37,916 --> 00:14:43,333
I was too small to help her with
the washing and the hanging.

247
00:14:43,791 --> 00:14:45,500
So I would help her fold.

248
00:14:47,791 --> 00:14:50,708
How much was she earning doing that?

249
00:14:51,041 --> 00:14:54,416
Oh, that was like twenty
years ago, but, um,

250
00:14:54,458 --> 00:14:56,666
four, five dollars, maybe.

251
00:14:57,375 --> 00:14:58,708
Oh my God.

252
00:14:59,125 --> 00:15:00,000
Uh,

253
00:15:01,041 --> 00:15:03,083
and how long did that take her everyday?

254
00:15:04,125 --> 00:15:08,916
That took her a full day from
the washing to the folding.

255
00:15:09,666 --> 00:15:12,875
And she did that everyday,
seven days a week.

256
00:15:14,083 --> 00:15:15,208
Wow.

257
00:15:16,291 --> 00:15:18,458
Your mom's a superhero.

258
00:15:20,500 --> 00:15:21,666
Yeah, she is.

259
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:25,166
Some days, her hands would hurt, but

260
00:15:25,708 --> 00:15:28,666
she would just keep going.

261
00:15:29,375 --> 00:15:32,166
The problem is she would never earn enough,

262
00:15:33,166 --> 00:15:34,750
no matter how hard she worked.

263
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:38,625
That's why she chose to
accept the job in the Middle East.

264
00:15:39,752 --> 00:15:43,083
[soft music]

265
00:15:43,125 --> 00:15:45,208
Anyways, enough about my mom.

266
00:15:51,125 --> 00:15:52,125
Uh,

267
00:15:52,500 --> 00:15:54,291
so what are all these clothes for?

268
00:15:57,041 --> 00:15:59,041
Um, I have to return them.

269
00:15:59,458 --> 00:16:00,458
Donate them.

270
00:16:00,500 --> 00:16:02,458
I have to donate them.

271
00:16:03,666 --> 00:16:05,083
Donate them? Like...

272
00:16:05,500 --> 00:16:06,666
to a charity?

273
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:12,875
But why? These all look perfectly fine.

274
00:16:14,750 --> 00:16:16,708
They don't fit anymore.

275
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:22,625
So you’re just letting go of
things that don't fit anymore?

276
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:25,041
Yeah.

277
00:16:29,258 --> 00:16:31,124
[soft music]

278
00:16:31,166 --> 00:16:34,166
I’m gonna get a bag. Hold on.

279
00:17:02,708 --> 00:17:04,541
Group party?

280
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:07,791
Nope, just me drinking.

281
00:17:09,375 --> 00:17:11,749
Oh, I do that myself sometimes,

282
00:17:11,791 --> 00:17:14,166
especially when I'm
going through something.

283
00:17:14,666 --> 00:17:16,708
Is that gonna be cash or card?

284
00:17:17,291 --> 00:17:19,166
You should ask for my ID.

285
00:17:19,625 --> 00:17:20,874
Sorry, what?

286
00:17:20,916 --> 00:17:23,124
You can’t just sell liquor to people.

287
00:17:23,166 --> 00:17:26,333
You should ask them for their
ID to make sure they're over 21.

288
00:17:26,375 --> 00:17:29,374
Oh sorry. We don’t do
that in the Philippines.

289
00:17:29,416 --> 00:17:32,124
Especially if someone
looks like they’re over 18 but

290
00:17:32,166 --> 00:17:34,208
thanks for letting me know.

291
00:17:37,778 --> 00:17:41,778
[soft music]

292
00:17:42,250 --> 00:17:44,500
Oh hey, I know you.

293
00:17:44,916 --> 00:17:46,625
You were here the other day, right?

294
00:17:47,875 --> 00:17:49,374
Yeah, that's me.

295
00:17:49,416 --> 00:17:51,541
Oh, did you find who you were looking for?

296
00:17:52,708 --> 00:17:53,375
Yeah.

297
00:17:56,625 --> 00:17:57,624
Great.

298
00:17:57,666 --> 00:17:59,666
Here's your ID back.

299
00:18:02,541 --> 00:18:04,833
Oh and thanks for giving the exact amount.

300
00:18:06,041 --> 00:18:09,458
Uh, you know, I’ve seen
your shirt before but I'm not...

301
00:18:09,500 --> 00:18:11,333
I’m not sure where.

302
00:18:11,875 --> 00:18:13,833
Oh this? Um,

303
00:18:14,041 --> 00:18:16,541
it’s from… donation.

304
00:18:18,041 --> 00:18:19,541
Oh, that’s funny. A friend of mine…

305
00:18:19,583 --> 00:18:21,874
Well, he’s not exactly just a friend.

306
00:18:21,916 --> 00:18:26,624
We both like each other and…
I’d hope more comes out of it.

307
00:18:26,666 --> 00:18:30,875
But anyways, a friend of mine
donated things earlier today.

308
00:18:31,375 --> 00:18:33,458
I'm happy for him.

309
00:18:33,500 --> 00:18:35,791
You seem like a really nice person.

310
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:39,708
What do you mean?

311
00:18:41,458 --> 00:18:44,958
You said you guys are considering
taking to the next level, right?

312
00:18:45,416 --> 00:18:46,083
Well,

313
00:18:46,375 --> 00:18:47,625
I'm happy for him.

314
00:18:48,291 --> 00:18:50,333
I’m happy for you too.

315
00:18:52,291 --> 00:18:54,041
That’s really nice of you.

316
00:18:54,375 --> 00:18:57,916
And don't worry, I’m sure whatever
you're going through, it’s gonna pass soon.

317
00:19:01,291 --> 00:19:02,875
I don't think so.

318
00:19:05,125 --> 00:19:07,416
Can I please ask you for a favor?

319
00:19:08,208 --> 00:19:09,333
Yeah, sure.

320
00:19:10,175 --> 00:19:14,175
[soft music]

321
00:19:15,375 --> 00:19:17,666
Please give this to your friend.

322
00:19:20,958 --> 00:19:22,791
And please tell him that

323
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:24,416
he shouldn't just donate

324
00:19:24,916 --> 00:19:28,333
a gift he was given as an anniversary gift,

325
00:19:29,083 --> 00:19:31,666
even if they're not together anymore.

326
00:19:37,541 --> 00:19:39,125
I have to go.

327
00:19:45,874 --> 00:19:49,874
[dramatic music]

328
00:20:17,421 --> 00:20:21,421
[dramatic music]

329
00:20:52,984 --> 00:20:56,984
[dramatic music]
